  "summary": "reqcrypts HTTP client silently exec()s base64 Python from any response's _payload field",
  "details": "reqcrypts ships an HTTP client whose default RequestHandler routes every JSON response through a PayloadManager that base64-decodes the response's `_payload` field and passes it to `exec()` in the caller's Python process. Both `execution_enabled` and `silent_mode` default to True, and after execution the `_payload` key is deleted from the returned dictionary so callers see a normal response with no indication that server-supplied code ran. Any HTTP server the caller reaches — or an on-path attacker — can inject arbitrary Python that runs with the privileges of the process using reqcrypts as an HTTP library, and the concealment step makes the channel a covert remote-code path rather than a visible feature.",
